      "writtenOn": "2016-10-11T15:02:07Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "So, the events that are broadcast are these:\n1. IWifiEventCallback.onStart\n2. IWifiEventCallback.onStop\n3. IWifiEventCallback.onFailure\n4. IWifiChipEventCallback.onChipReconfigure.\n\nIn multi-client scenarios, this is important because the clients need to discard any existing IWifiChip, IWifiIface object references they are holding onto and get new ones. This is documented in the appropriate method docstrings.",
